<title>USA: FGIC qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies six muni issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance co said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following six municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Peoria County, Ill., $12.01 million general obligation bonds, by direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Grant County, Ind., $4.85 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Readington Township Board of Education, N.J., $12 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Henderson, Nev., $26.075 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Cobleskill-Rich Central School District, N.Y., $4.7 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Washington, $245.82 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
